        "id": "ethics",
        "title": "Responsibility & ethics",
        "text": "04 - Ethics A research agenda, not a conclusion Interview preparation identifies the remaining agenda: field burden and the existing diagnostic workflow; sampling representativeness; false positives; discrimination between harmful and free-living nematodes; the relevant decision makers; responsible control after a result; and regulatory and implementation questions. These are planned lines of inquiry, not completed consultations or validated requirements. Education is a separate stream of documented activity. It is not stakeholder consultation or product validation, and it cannot close an input-to-design loop. Names and direct quotations are withheld because the reviewed files do not document public-attribution consent. This describes missing documentation only; the status is simply unverified. Current documented status The evidence supports documented consultation, an unanalysed questionnaire stream, and unresolved questions. No verified integrated Human Practices cycle is documented yet.",
